{"type": "thinking", "text": "Now the second line vanished and line 1 focused. It seems the scratchpad's second line was a temporary \"new line\" that disappears when keyboard opens? Hmm. In these apps, the last line is a \"new line\" placeholder. When you tap it and type, but somehow no effect.\n\nWait now only 1 line total. Did the type_text clear the second line? The typed \"b = 2\" is nowhere. Weird. Maybe type_text clears the field and enters text, but the field (empty line) got deleted because... Hmm.\n\nLet's think about this app's behavior. Maybe there's a \"line numbers\" gutter: [0] View \"1\", [1] EditText \"a = 10\", [3] View \"2\", [4] EditText empty. It's a list. Tapping the empty last line focuses it. Maybe typing in it triggers a rebuild that loses characters because of \"simpler evaluation pass on every edit\".\n\nThis could be a genuine bug: the new evaluation pass on every edit breaks typing in the scratchpad/file! But wait, other files have data saved and we didn't test typing. Let me test typing in a proper file: e.g., tap line 1 of some file, append \" + 1\" using keyboard keys. Hmm.\n\nActually, maybe the issue is that type_text enters the whole string via a single setText and the EditText's watcher resets it. Let's try typing character by character using press_key? press_key supports ENTER, DEL etc. but not letters. Hmm, type_text is the only way to type.\n\nLet me try a simple thing: tap on line 1 \"a = 10\" to place cursor, then type_text \" \" maybe. Let's test what happens with a single char.\n\nAlternatively, maybe it's the keyboard suggestion strip stealing events. Let's test in a real file instead.\n\nActually, let me reconsider: the observe after type_text with element=4 shows line 1 focused and keyboard shown. It's like the second line was not real, and tapping it focused line 1? No, before the tap, [4] was the empty second line. After type, [37] EditText \"a = 10\" focused.\n\nHmm wait, maybe I misread: In observe after tapping element 4, [40] EditText empty focused was line 2. Then type_text \"b = a * 2\" resulted in [38] EditText \"b = a * 2a = 10\". So line 2 became \"b = a * 2a = 10\" and line 1 vanished. Then undo restored.\n\nThen type_text with element=4 now: maybe element numbering changed and element 4 is line 1? No, after undo the observe listed [1] EditText \"a = 10\", [4] EditText empty. So element 4 was empty line 2. type_text tapped it and typed \"b = 2\" resulting in... [37] EditText \"a = 10\" focused, one line.\n\nSo typed text vanished. Possibly because after typing \"b\" the eval pass decided line \"b\" is incomplete and removed it? Or the empty second line is a \"new line\" that only becomes real if the last character is submitted (Enter)?\n\nIn the first attempt without submit, the result was line \"b = a * 2a = 10\" i.e. the new line merged with old. Ugh.\n\nMaybe the app's editor works like: there is one EditText per line, and the \"empty\" last line is a placeholder for adding new line. When you type into it, it should create a new line. But the eval pass \"on every edit\" might reset focus to the previous line, causing subsequent characters to go there... Actually the typed chars ended up in the wrong order.\n\nThis is likely a genuine bug introduced: \"assignments are now resolved from top to bottom by a simpler evaluation pass on every edit\" — the pass on every edit might rebuild the list and mess up focus/cursor, leading to text scrambling. But we need a clean reproduction with real user-like typing.\n\nLet me try again more slowly, typing one character at a time to see. But type_text types the whole string at once (via adb input?). It could be that the text insertion is done by setting the text in one go and the app's TextWatcher triggers. Hmm.\n\nLet's test with a different method: use the on-screen keyboard keys via tap. The Gboard keys are elements with desc. Tapping \"b\" etc. But each tap is one call. Typing \"b = 2\" would be ~5 calls. Doable.\n\nActually, easier: let me test in an existing file where I can append to an existing line. E.g., Percentages file line 1 \"price = 240\". Tap at end, then use type_text \" + 10\" maybe. Let's see if it works. Actually we can add a new line by pressing ENTER at end of an existing line then typing.\n\nBut first, maybe I should reproduce the \"variables\" bug more directly with existing files. The \"Monthly budget\" file has variable references: total = salary+bonus presumably, grand_total = total(gift)+? Let's inspect the actual expressions. The EditText shows only \"total\", not expanded. Hmm.\n\nWait, in the Monthly budget, line 3 is \"total\" (keyword), not \"total = salary + bonus\". So \"total\" is a special operator that sums above? And grand_total? Hmm, \"grand_total\" maybe special too? Let me reconsider: The precondition says \"salary = 2500, bonus = 300.5, total, a blank line, gift = 49.5, total, grand_total\". So there are three totals. \"total\" lines sum the preceding values (within segment separated by blank lines? or all above). grand_total maybe sum of all totals? Hmm.\n\nActually NerdCalci docs: I recall a calculator app where writing `total` sums all numbers above; a `sum` keyword etc. Let me check the \"What's New\" for hints.\n\nLet me check What's New. But first, the % bug is clear. Let's gather more evidence.\n\nLet me go back to home and check What's New."}
