{"type": "thinking", "text": "Pin and lock persist across backgrounding. Good.\n\nNow maybe test rotate while in a locked file / pinned home. Let's rotate to landscape and observe.\n\nActually first, let me check whether the % bug is the only one. Let me test other percent semantics in the scratchpad to see if the new rule introduces more wrong results. I'll reopen scratchpad and test:\n- `200 + 10%` → 220\n- `200 - 10%` → 180\n- `200 * 10%` → 20? or 2000%?\n- `10 % 3` → error (bug)\n- `100 % 13` → error.\n- `50% of 200` → 100.\n- `disc% off price` kind.\n\nMaybe also `%` after a closing paren: `(100) % 13`. \n\nBut the report about modulo is enough. However maybe the intended bug is different: e.g. `20% of 250` now returns 50%? no it's correct.\n\nHmm, maybe the \"new rule\" is supposed to interpret `x%` as a percentage *only when followed by of/off* or in arithmetic. The bug: `%` between operands (modulo) is broken. That's the finding. Let me also test `19.5 % 4` etc. Already error.\n\nLet me also check the precedence `250 + 20%` = 300 vs expected maybe 250.2. The file's line 6 result 300. If the intended new rule is \"a % after an operand is a percentage of the left operand\" then 250+20% = 300 is right. In NerdCalci docs, `%` is \"percentage\": e.g., `200 + 10%` = 220. Yes, 300 is likely right. So only modulo broken.\n\nNow pin/lock bug search. Let me consider the \"modified timestamp changes\" more. When I pinned Temperatures at 12:06, its MODIFIED became \"12:06 PM\". Before pinning it was JAN 08, 2026. That's clearly a change of the displayed last-modified time due to a pin operation (not content). Is this a bug worth reporting? It affects the \"newest first\" ordering: pinning/locking causes the file to be considered newly modified. If the app sorts by modified desc, that's a side effect. But pinned files are at top anyway, so maybe not user-visible in pinned section. But once unpinned, it stays at top of ALL FILES (Temperatures unpinned jumped to top with 12:07). That could be considered \"wrong_value\" on MODIFIED. Hmm.\n\nBut wait, maybe this is intentional: \"MODIFIED\" could mean \"file record last modified (metadata)\" which includes pin/lock. Hmm. However, when editing content, modified time changes too. Ambiguous.\n\nLet's look for a more clear-cut pin bug. Consider: \"pinned files are now kept at the top of the list.\" Test on Search: Search maybe lists results and pinned should still top. Let's test search. Tap Search [18], type \"e\" maybe to see. Search requires typing; use type_text (single word works better). Let's see.\n\nActually, maybe the pin bug is that the pinned file is shown in the PINNED section *and* sorted by modified, but \"kept at the top of the list\" might mean within the existing order rather than a separate section. That's fine.\n\nAnother idea: maybe \"lock\" bug is that a locked file can still be renamed or deleted? We saw disabled. Duplicate is enabled which is fine.\n\nMaybe lock bug: lock state indicator disappears after pinning/unpinning? We saw it persists.\n\nMaybe lock bug: opening a locked file from the *global file* or from search bypasses lock? Search just opens.\n\nMaybe lock bug: if you lock a file while it's open in the editor (via More options in editor)? The editor's More options might allow locking? Let's check the file editor's More options menu [19]. It might have \"Pin\"/\"Lock\" too. If locking from within the editor leaves editing enabled, that's a bug. Let's inspect.\n\nCurrently on home. Open a file (not locked), e.g., Temperature sums, then check More options. But maybe the editor's More options has a \"Lock\" option. Let's test on Temperature sums (unlocked). Open it and check menu.\n\nActually, the changed build note specifically says \"Home screen pin and lock controls\", so controls are on home.\n\nHmm, wait. Another angle: \"pinned files are now kept at the top of the list\" — what if you pin a file while the sort order is Ascending by name? We tested Name Descending. Let's test Name Ascending with pin. If pinned moves out of top, bug. But likely fine.\n\nLet's test Search with pinned. Tap Search [18]."}
