{"type": "text", "text": "The QA sweep is complete and I've signed off. Summary of what I did and found:\n\n## Found & logged (confirmed)\n**Modulo `%` operator broken — Remainders file**\n- `100 % 13` → **Err** (expected 9)\n- `47 % 20` → **Err** (expected 7)\n- `19.5 % 4` → **Err** (expected 3.5)\n- `a % 14` with `a = 50` → **Err** (expected 8)\n- Error tooltip: \"Unexpected number\" — the new `%` parsing consumes `100 %` as a percentage token and rejects the right operand.\n- `250 + 20%` = 300 still works, so only modulo is affected.\n- Developer confirmed and logged it.\n\n## Verified working (no defects)\n- **Operators/percentages:** Expenses (1,625.75 / 541.92), Percentages (36, 204, 8.50, 102, 8), unit math in Temperatures (-53.89 °C), Temperature sums (2.22 °C), number bases, date/time gap arithmetic all correct.\n- **Variables:** assignments resolve strictly top-to-bottom on every edit; dependent lines recalculate immediately; undefined/forward references error correctly; re-assignments and block-scoped `total`/`avg`/`grand_total` behave correctly.\n- **Pinning/locking:** pinned files stay in a PINNED section at the top across all sort modes, rotation, backgrounding and rename; unpinning restores the file and removes the empty header; locked files are read-only (edits, rename, delete, clear all blocked) and the lock persists across navigation/search/background/rotation.\n\nI also observed (and reported twice, but the developer could not reproduce) that pinning/locking refreshes a file's \"MODIFIED\" timestamp and thus moves it to the top of the date-sorted list after unpinning."}
